<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Samsung spins off two sub-groups.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Samsung spins off two sub-groups.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Samsung Group, South Korea's second largest conglomerate, said on Friday it has spun off Cheiljedang Corp and Shinsegae Department Store .</p>
<p>A group spokesman said the number of Samsung Group subsidiaries fell to 59 from 80 with the separation.</p>
<p>Cheiljedang, a food and chemical company, is a sub-group company which has 10 subsidiaries, while Shinsegae holds 21 firms.</p>
</text>
